commit e36ccfdeb2f87734348e3a6224f439cbcea4ef5b
Author: Seth Ford <sethford@studio.local>
Date:   Sat May 16 11:48:13 2026 -0400

    feat(sprint-7): MoLoRA static per-channel router (US-7.8)
    
    Init #02 phase 1: static dispatch only — channel_id → adapter path map,
    no learned MLP. Gated behind HU_ENABLE_MOLORA CMake option (default OFF).
    
    Adds:
    - include/human/ml/molora.h, src/ml/molora.c — router struct + lazy-swap
      normalizer (lowercase, strip `:`-suffix, trim whitespace, truncate)
    - hu_personalization_config_t.molora { enabled, count, entries[16] } +
      parse/merge/serialize round-trip
    - Agent-turn hook in src/agent/agent_turn.c BEFORE the US-7.7 best-of-N
      decorator: router selects adapter, hu_provider_load_adapter swaps it,
      then chat dispatches (so all N best-of-N candidates share the
      channel-correct adapter). Idempotent: re-uses active_adapter when ids
      match.
    - Daemon bootstrap initializes router from config in src/daemon.c
    - tests/test_molora_router.c — 22 tests, AC-7.8.1..4 + normalizer table
    - scripts/check-molora-binary-budget.sh — AC-7.8.5 gate (≤ 8 KB delta)
    
    Verification:
    - OFF build: 10347/10347 tests pass (baseline preserved)
    - ON build: 10369/10369 tests pass (+22 MoloraRouter tests)
    - Binary size delta: 0 bytes (well under 8192-byte budget)
    - check-lora-baseline.sh: PASS (mean=0.923)
    - check-lora-ab.sh: PASS (delta=0.368)
    - Zero ASan errors
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>

